      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Miike Domain — the maru-marker opening this domain's entry. Miike was a 10,000-koku domain in Chikugo province held by the Tachibana house. Everything to the marker's right is the tail of the preceding domain (Mikusa); everything to its left, as far as the ○靜岡藩 marker, is Miike's."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "三池藩マル記號"
